() Tj T*
(Here are the lines he meant:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Berries already, September soon,--) Tj T*
(The shortening day and ike early moon;) Tj T*
(The year is busy with next year's flowers) Tj T*
(The seeds are ready for next year' showers;) Tj T*
(Through a thousand tossing trees there swells) Tj T*
(The sigh of the Summer's sad farewells.) Tj T*
(Too soon those leaves in the sunset sky) Tj T*
(Low down on the wintry ground will lie,) Tj T*
(And grim November and December) Tj T*
(Leave naught of Summer to remember--) Tj T*
(Saving some flower in a book put by,) Tj T*
(Secure from the soft effacing snow,) Tj T*
(Though all the rest of the Summer go._) Tj T*
