(wayside letter-boxes, in such names, for instance, as "Theo. Leveque" and) Tj T*
("Paul Fugle," which, like wind-blown exotics from other lands, we found) Tj T*
(within a few yards of each other. One name, that of "Silvernail," we) Tj T*
(decided could only lawfully belong to a princess in a fairy tale. Such) Tj T*
(childishness as this, I may say, is of the essence of a walking trip, in) Tj T*
(which, from moment to moment, you take quite infantile interest in all) Tj T*
(manner of idle observation and quite useless lore. That is a part of the) Tj T*
(game you are playing, and the main thing is that you are out in the open) Tj T*
(air, on the open road, with a simple heart and a romantic appetite.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
