(sketching one of those ruined farms:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Apples along the highway strewn,) Tj T*
(  And morning opening all her doors;) Tj T*
(The cawing rook, the distant train,) Tj T*
(  The valley with its misty floors;) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The hillside hung with woods and dreams,) Tj T*
(  Soft gleams of gossamer and dew;) Tj T*
(From cockcrow to the rising moon) Tj T*
(  The rainbowed road for me and you.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Along the highroad all the day) Tj T*
(  The wagons filled with apples go,) Tj T*
