(So long, so long, has man pursued these ancient tasks; so long ago was) Tj T*
(he urging the plowshare through the furrow, so long ago the sower went) Tj T*
(forth to sow; so long ago have there been barns and byres, granaries and) Tj T*
(threshing-floors, mills and vineyards; so long has there been milking of) Tj T*
(cows, and herding of sheep and swine. Can one see a field of wheat) Tj T*
