(aloud from its consecrated pages:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
("_I can repeat to thee many a counsel of them of old, if thou shrink not) Tj T*
(back nor weary to learn of lowly cares. Above all must the) Tj T*
(threshing-floor be levelled with the ponderous roller, and wrought by) Tj T*
(hand and cemented with clinging potter's clay, that it may not gather) Tj T*
(weeds nor crack in the reign of dust, and be playground withal for) Tj T*
(manifold destroyers. Often the tiny mouse builds his house and makes his) Tj T*
(granaries underground, or the eyeless mole scoops his cell; and in chinks) Tj T*
(is found the toad, and all the swarming vermin that are bred in earth;) Tj T*
(and the weevil, and the ant that fears a destitute old age, plunder the) Tj T*
(great pile of spelt_.") Tj T*
