(Nature had planted stern thickets of oak-trees along the rocky edge, and) Tj T*
("the acorns of our lord of Chaonia" crunched beneath our feet as we) Tj T*
(walked on.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After a while, sure enough we came upon "Billy the Cobbler," seated at) Tj T*
(his bench in a little shop at the beginning of a straggle of houses,) Tj T*
(alone, save for his cat, at the sleepy end of afternoon. We had) Tj T*
(understood that he had been crippled in some cruel accident of machinery,) Tj T*
(and was hampered in the use of his legs. But, unless in a certain) Tj T*
(philosophic sweetness on his big, happy face, there was no sign of the) Tj T*
