(mazy lines, some faint and wayward as a hair, and some straight and) Tj T*
(decided as a steel track--whence and whither do they lead? I love the map) Tj T*
(best when the journey is done--when I can pore on its lines as into the) Tj T*
(lined face of some dear friend with whom I have travelled the years, and) Tj T*
(say--here this happened, here that befell! This almost invisible dot is) Tj T*
(made of magic rocks and is filled with the song of rapids; this) Tj T*
(infinitesimal fraction of "Scale five miles to the inch" is a haunted) Tj T*
(valley of purple pine-woods, and the moon rising, and the lonely cry of a) Tj T*
(sheep that has lost her little one somewhere in the folds of the hills.) Tj T*
(Here, where is no name, stands an old white church with a gilded cross,) Tj T*
(among little white houses huddled together under a bluff. In yonder) Tj T*
(garden the priest's cassock and trousers are hanging sacrilegiously on a) Tj T*
(clothes-line, and you can just see a tiny graveyard away up on the) Tj T*
(hillside almost hidden in the trees.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
