(vagabond ethics necessitate our conscientiously tramping every foot of) Tj T*
(these "gritty paving-stones," we asked each other, as we entered upon a) Tj T*
(region of depressing suburbs, and we called a halt on the spot to discuss) Tj T*
(the point. The discussion was not long, and it was brought to a) Tj T*
(cheerful, demoralized end by the approach of the trolley, into which,) Tj T*
(regardless of right or wrong, we climbed with alacrity, not to alight) Tj T*
(till not only Elmira was left behind, but more weary suburbs, too, on the) Tj T*
(other side. That night, as old travellers phrase it, we lay at Waverly,) Tj T*
(on the frontier of Pennsylvania, a sad, dirty little town, grotesquely) Tj T*
(belying its romantic name, and only surpassed in squalor by the) Tj T*
(classically named Athens--beware, reader, of American towns named out of) Tj T*
(classical dictionaries! Here, however, our wanderings in the) Tj T*
(brick-and-mortar wilderness were to end, for by a long, romantic, old,) Tj T*
(covered bridge we crossed the Chemung River, and there once more, on the) Tj T*
(other side, was Nature, lovelier than ever, awaiting us. Not Dante, when) Tj T*
(he emerged from Hades and again beheld the stars, drew deeper breaths of) Tj T*
(escape than we, thus escaping from--Athens!) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(And soon we were to meet the Susquehanna--beautiful, broad-bosomed name,) Tj T*
(that has always haunted my imagination like the name of some beautiful) Tj T*
(savage princess--_La belle sauvage_. Susquehanna! What a southern) Tj T*
(opulence in the soft, seductive syllables! Yes, soon we were to meet the) Tj T*
(Susquehanna. Nor had we long to wait, and little did we suspect what our) Tj T*
(meeting with that beautiful river was to mean.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Chemung, on whose east bank we were now walking, seemed a noble) Tj T*
(enough river, very broad and all the more picturesque for being) Tj T*
(shallow with the Summer drought; and its shining reaches and wooded) Tj T*
ET
